  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moldova: Supporting Transparency and Ethics in the Prosecution Service (STEP): Moldova&#x2019;s Extraordinary Prosecutor Vetting Commission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To increase the ability of the Prosecutor Vetting Commission (PVC) to evaluate prosecutors. 2) To improve the capacity of PVC operations. 3) To enhance access to information for non-governmental organizations, intergovernmental organizations and the Moldovan public.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The Prosecutor Vetting Commission and its Secretariat. Indirect beneficiaries: Superior Council of Prosecutors, Office of the Prosecutor General, Moldova&#x2019;s anti-corruption institutions, prosecutors and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to increase public confidence and trust in the justice sector through the creation and functioning of the Prosecutor Vetting Commission.</narrative>
  </description>
